WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:06.800
Season 2 of Supergirl saw the show fly over
to the CW to join its fellow DC TV shows and

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:11.160
introduced a bunch of brilliant new characters
including Tyler Hoechlin as Superman, Floriana

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.930
Lima as Maggie Sawyer, and Chris Wood as Mon-El.

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:17.590
Yippee ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and in this video I'm going to break down

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:21.260
some of the coolest easter eggs and connections
to comic books, superhero shows and movies

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.490
that I found in season 2 of Supergirl.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:28.190
By the way, I've got an epic Super-Flarrow-verse
giveaway on my Supergirl, Flash, and Arrow

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:29.190
videos.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:32.590
For a chance to win any of these Funko Pops,
make sure you subscribe and leave a comment

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:35.360
about the show's easter eggs or season finale.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:39.140
Quick warning: there are spoilers ahead, so
if you want to avoid those, come back when

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.590
you've caught up with Season 2!

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:45.260
Now that the series has put a face to its
Man of Steel, there've been even more Superman

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:49.219
references this season, right from the opening
episode which was named The Adventures of

00:00:49.219 --> 00:00:55.180
Supergirl in tribute to the 1940s radio show,
1950s TV series, and later comic book series,

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:57.190
The Adventures of Superman.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:02.360
And that popular 1940s radio show also gave
us the phrase 'up, up, and away' when Superman

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.980
soared off into the skies.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:08.100
And that phrase gets an airing at the end
of episode 1 when Clark and Kara say it before

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.830
flying off together, and again in episode
21, when Cat Grant urges Supergirl to get

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:15.399
on with rescuing Mon-El and Lena Luthor.

00:01:15.399 --> 00:01:19.799
Speaking of Cat Grant, the way she reacts
when she sees Clark at CatCo and the fact

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:24.140
he says he has 'some sway with' her are playful
nods to the comic book series The Adventures

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:28.869
of Superman, where the gossip columnist Cat
first appeared in the late 1980s as a romantic

00:01:28.869 --> 00:01:30.749
partner for Clark Kent.

00:01:30.749 --> 00:01:34.979
And the name of Cat's new assistant, Miss
Teschmacher, is a shout-out to the first two

00:01:34.979 --> 00:01:38.779
Superman movies with Christopher Reeve where
Teschmacher was also the name of Lex Luther's

00:01:38.779 --> 00:01:40.950
assistant and love interest.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:45.639
And amusingly enough, Cat Grant shouts Miss
Teschmacher's name in the same way that Gene

00:01:45.639 --> 00:01:48.520
Hackman's Luthor did in those movies.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:53.729
In episode 15, after Kara's fired from CatCo,
she explains why she's upset to Mon-El, saying,

00:01:53.729 --> 00:01:57.469
'Supergirl is what I can do; Kara is who I
am'.

00:01:57.469 --> 00:02:02.359
This echoes Clark Kent's words to Lois Lane
in the second season of the 1990s TV series

00:02:02.359 --> 00:02:06.619
Lois &amp; Clark, which is brilliantly fitting
as not only does this episode of Supergirl

00:02:06.619 --> 00:02:11.900
feature Dean Cain but also Teri Hatcher, who
starred as Clark and Lois in that TV show.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:16.819
There are more cool references to iconic DC
characters in the episode 'Welcome to Earth',

00:02:16.819 --> 00:02:21.260
with an especially nice homage to Lynda Carter's
Wonder Woman when Supergirl is on fire and

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:24.849
puts out the flames by imitating Carter's
famous Wonder Woman spin.

00:02:24.849 --> 00:02:29.319
By the way, Lynda Carter, who plays President
Olivia Marsdin on the show, even gave Melissa

00:02:29.319 --> 00:02:33.010
Benoist some tips for the scene, showing her
how she did her classic twirl!

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:38.209
There's also another sly wink in that episode
to fans of Carter's Wonder Woman, when Supergirl

00:02:38.209 --> 00:02:42.140
says how impressed she is to have seen Air
Force One, and the President replies, 'if

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:46.719
you think that's cool, you ought to see my
other jet', a delicious reference to Wonder

00:02:46.719 --> 00:02:48.689
Woman's invisible jet!

00:02:48.689 --> 00:02:53.171
By the way, the President's name, Olivia Marsdin,
is also a little hat-tip to Olive Byrne, one

00:02:53.171 --> 00:02:57.930
of the inspirations behind Wonder Woman, and
to Wonder Woman's creator, William Moulton

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:58.930
Marston.

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:03.709
Oh, and the President's hairstyle in episodes
17 and 21 is a little throwback to Lynda Carter's

00:03:03.709 --> 00:03:06.780
look as Diana Prince in her 70s TV series.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:12.079
Mehcad Brooks got to suit up this season as
Jimmy Olsen took on the mantle of the Guardian,

00:03:12.079 --> 00:03:16.709
a DC character who first appeared in issue
7 of Star Spangled Comics when a cop called

00:03:16.709 --> 00:03:18.269
Jim Harper became a vigilante.

00:03:18.269 --> 00:03:23.209
And during Guardian's first appearance in
episode 6, there's a nod to his character's

00:03:23.209 --> 00:03:27.930
comic book origins thanks to Winn's van which
has the words Star Spangled Delivery Company

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:33.799
emblazoned on it, along with the year 1941,
which is when the first issue of Star Spangled

00:03:33.799 --> 00:03:34.799
Comics was published.

00:03:34.799 --> 00:03:39.980
Oh, and the number 204 on the van is a reference
to the last issue published in the retitled

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:41.810
Star Spangled [War Stories] series.

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:46.840
Plus, in the following episode, Guardian catches
a thief who's just robbed a store called Newsboy,

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:50.860
which is a shout-out to the Newsboy Legion,
a boy gang who appeared alongside Guardian

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:52.590
in the comics.

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:57.159
The title of the mid-season premiere, "Supergirl
Lives" is a shout-out to the episode's director

00:03:57.159 --> 00:04:02.069
Kevin Smith and his script for the abandoned
1990s movie "Superman Lives", which was going

00:04:02.069 --> 00:04:05.209
to be directed by Tim Burton and star Nic
Cage as Superman.

00:04:05.209 --> 00:04:09.569
And there's another sneaky reference to that
cancelled film when Mon-El tells Supergirl

00:04:09.569 --> 00:04:13.560
that the alien Jo Gunraf is cooking up Thanagarian
snarebeast.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:17.750
When Kevin Smith was developing the Superman
Lives script, producer Jon Peters insisted

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:22.130
there should be a scene where Superman battled
a giant spider, and the planned name for that

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:25.180
spider was a Thanagarian Snare Beast.

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:29.080
Season 2's also brought us a nice sprinkling
of Batman references.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:33.560
In the Fortress of Solitude, just before Supergirl
sets the Atomic Cauldron to blow up herself

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:38.160
and Mr Mxyzptlk, she tells the fifth-dimensional
imp that she's had enough of his games, and

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:39.520
adds, 'You wanna get nuts?

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:40.910
Let's get nuts!'

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:45.840
That line is straight from Tim Burton's 1989
Batman movie and was said by Michael Keaton's

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:49.210
Bruce Wayne as he flew into a rage with the
Joker.

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:53.449
And in episode 20, City of Lost Children,
there's a humorous nod to the Caped Crusader

00:04:53.449 --> 00:04:57.509
and the Man of Steel's fraught relationship
in both the comics and the movie, Batman vs

00:04:57.509 --> 00:05:01.789
Superman: Dawn of Justice, when James laments
that people he tries to help are scared by

00:05:01.789 --> 00:05:03.470
his Guardian outfit.

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:07.800
'People see this big guy in a scary mask and
they run away, just like Clark's friend,'

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:08.800
says James.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:11.500
To which Winn replies, '… I feel like they're
more frenemies.'

